# Rust (Talaria workspace)

## Layout

- `talaria-api`: HTTP, person ingest (`person_ingest/`), routes.
- `talaria-store`: SQLx, migrations (embedded — rebuild after new `migrations/*.sql`).
- `talaria-quality`: gates, occurrence keys, grounding.
- `talaria-sources`: connectors and extractors.
- Offline dump chain (`talaria-dump`, `talaria-cosmos`) writes `pipeline='legacy'`; explorer uses `pipeline='person'` only.

## Changes

- Prefer explicit errors and existing domain types; small functions; avoid new deps unless necessary.
- After edits: `cargo check -p <crate>`; for substantive work `cargo test -p talaria-quality` and/or `cargo test -p talaria-sources` (fixtures, no network).

## SQL

No `TRUNCATE` in migrations. Destructive person-pipeline rebuild is CLI-only (`talaria admin rebuild-person-pipeline --confirm-destruction`).
